@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Native serif glyph construction and rest registration boundary (WIP)
+
+serif_glyphs::build implements dy=0 lookup, section-width filtering, stable abscissa order, BarFilamentFactory core height/centroid admission and iterative touching section attachment. It builds canonical VERTICAL foreground runs from the full accepted section union. Actual vLag/hLag sections within system bounds must be supplied by the caller. No fabricated glyph is substituted when the original core has no filament.
+
+48 newly captured independent direct original filament controls cover interline 15/16/17, threshold heights, vertical and horizontal sections, core-edge positions and attachments. Native matches all 32 accepted glyphs (bounds, orientation and every foreground pixel) and all 16 rejections. These are supplied-section factory/toGlyph controls, not uninterrupted complete-rest conversion controls. The Java observer executes unchanged original methods and never reads native outputs.
+
+RestGraph::register creates explicit phase-local rest vertices, then LEFT/RIGHT serif vertices and relations in plan encounter order, preserving beam grade, median, height and staff plus serif impacts/median/width. Glyph identity uses the existing canonical registry without adding glyph groups. Plans are checked and glyphs built before graph mutation. Registry budget failure can leave partial registration; finish_cleanup rejects incomplete relation sets. Graph records are an explicit boundary, not full shared-SIG/CLI integration or Java global identity equivalence.
+
+finish_cleanup runs separately after all successful registrations. It removes real SystemCandidates through their tombstone API, prunes incident exclusions, updates GroupPass membership/bounds/supports without regrouping, preserves surviving group identity/member order, drops empty ensembles, and retains beam glyphs. 16 newly captured independent original populateSystem + Inter.remove controls match surviving group bounds/member/support order. These controls cover singleton and 2/3/4-member groups with none/first/last/all removals. Wider exclusion, bridge and intertwined-group scenarios remain uncovered. A native integration test verifies candidate tombstones, exclusions, group identity/bounds and glyph retention together with graph registration; other graph tests check ordered IDs/relations, canonical glyph reuse and missing-filament rejection.
+
+15 focused tests, fmt and all-targets Clippy pass. Inherited 75 original serif-side and 103 original group controls remain unchanged. Exact fresh restore verifies the full source checkpoint chain. Current full regression is UNVERIFIED, deferred to a meaningful integrated rest pipeline boundary. Complete original positive/negative rest conversion controls, actual staff/lag mapping, shared SIG identity, real-score conversion, epilog and CLI wiring remain unfinished. Full OMR remains unfinished.
